  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify sender, check mailbox usage and devices per KB-009"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0101",
  "reason": "KB-009 quick check: confirm laptop is online"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for reporting this. Your mailbox isn't the problem: it's only about 17% full, and your phone is getting new mail. Your laptop is also online and connected. That points to Outlook on the laptop itself. Please try these steps in order and check for new mail after each one:\n\n1. Open Outlook on the web in your browser and check that today's mail is there. If it isn't there either, let us know right away.\n2. In Outlook on your laptop, go to the Send / Receive tab. If 'Work Offline' is highlighted, click it to turn it off.\n3. Close Outlook completely and open it again.\n4. Restart your laptop.\n5. If it's still stuck, set up a fresh Outlook profile. Open Control Panel, then Mail, then Show Profiles. Click Add, create a new profile, set it as the default, and open Outlook. Your mail will download again, which can take a little while.\n\nPlease reply to let us know whether Outlook on the web shows your new mail and which step fixed it. If none of them work, reply and we'll pass this to a senior engineer. If it's easier, we can also walk you through the profile step by phone.",
  "internal_note": "User: Dana Whitfield (CEO, VIP), user_id 1. Outlook on the laptop stopped syncing this morning. Mobile mail works. Checks per KB-009: mailbox is 17.4% used (8,900 of 51,200 MB), so KB-010 doesn't apply. Laptop BL-LT-0101 is online, last check-in 2026-10-09 15:03 UTC, 60% disk free, no warnings. Account is active and not locked. Mobile working means the mailbox and service are healthy, so this looks like a problem with the Outlook client on the laptop. Sent the user the KB-009 user-side steps: confirm mail in Outlook on the web, turn off Work Offline, restart Outlook, restart the laptop, rebuild the profile. No other reports of this issue, so no sign of an outage. Escalate to Tier 2 if Outlook on the web also lacks new mail (per KB-009) or if the profile rebuild doesn't fix it. User is VIP, so consider offering a callback to help with the profile rebuild.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
